2026-10-17T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2320) 'how it is set up, and what it leaves out
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2320  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-17T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2320) 'An agent drives the OXRSys Simulator on the Mac through cua-driver's own MCP server, registered under the name `xr-cua-oxrsys`. It launches the simulator, reads the decoded preview as pixels and the control row as accessibility elements, and sends keys, clicks, typing and scrolls into the view. Every call runs in the background: no focus change and no cursor move, so the operator keeps working in another window. The operator ruled it done on 2026-10-17.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2320  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-17T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2320) '- RFD66606-2235, the agent that plans with taskweft through the editor, done in desktop mode through XR Pilot's plan tool.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2320  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-17T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2320) 'Setup
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2320  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-17T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2320) 'cua-driver is installed once on the Mac and reused across projects. Its accessibility and screen-recording grants belong to the driver app, not to the terminal that runs the agent. `scripts/xr-cua-oxrsys-register.sh` writes the `xr-cua-oxrsys` entry (command `cua-driver`, argument `mcp`) into the agent's MCP settings, keeps every other server and prints the diff. A running session picks the entry up when it reconnects its MCP servers.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2320  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-17T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2320) 'Where it landed
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2320  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-17T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2320) 'XR Pilot's repository, commit "Add xr-cua-oxrsys as the automation surface for the simulator" (2026-10-01): the document and the installer, 91 lines in two files. The plan tool landed there in "Add a plan tool that acts out a taskweft RECTGTN task network" (2026-10-04).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2320  1 LINE
 Text:Written

